WEBVTT

NOTE Edited transcription of a historical recording. Unclear speech is marked; use current specifications for ordering.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.400
Welcome to this training on appliance cabinet
cutouts with WW Wood Products cabinetry.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:09.100
In this session, we'll walk through the
different types of cutouts available,

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:14.000
the construction styles, and how to properly
design and order them. Whether you're working

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.500
with Shiloh or Eclipse cabinetry, this guide
will help you get it right the first time.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:24.200
An appliance cutout simply means that a portion
of the cabinet is modified to fit in appliance.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:29.200
Common examples include ovens, built-in
microwaves, and warming drawers.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:33.000
The type of construction you choose determines
how the appliance will sit in the cabinet.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:38.900
In standard construction, the appliance opening
is created using a 3 quarter inch overlay front

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:44.800
panel. The appliance sits in front of this
panel. In Eclipse frameless construction, the
same effect

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:49.400
can be achieved without an overlay panel, and
the appliance will sit against the box of the
cabinet

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:55.200
which will feel a bit more streamlined. Flush
inset construction is different. It also uses an

00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:00.700
overlay panel. But here, the cutout surrounds
the outside of the appliance, so the front

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:05.300
of the appliance is flush with the face of the
cabinet. This is the most built-in option

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:09.900
where the appliance will not be proud of the
front of the cabinet. This flush-inset
construction

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:14.600
can be used in both Shiloh Framed and Eclipse
Frameless cabinet designs.

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:16.400
Types of Appliance Cabinets

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:21.500
Appliance cabinets are available in wall, base,
and tall cabinet configurations, and

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:29.400
come in multiple depths—18, 21, 24—and in select
utility oven cabinets, even 27 and

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:35.500
30 inches. These size options give you
flexibility to match your appliance
specifications.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:37.900
Tall oven cabinets—universal

00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:44.200
In Shiloh Cabinetry, you can choose universal
oven cabinets, labeled OUF and OMUF. These

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:50.000
do not come with a specific cutout size.
Instead, you modify them in the field. The
height is

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:55.100
modified by removing drawer components and
trimming up to 6.5 inches from the oven opening

00:01:55.100 --> 00:02:00.800
header. Width adjustments are made by trimming
and attaching the included 1.5 inch fillers.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:05.700
The floor is a [thickness unclear] plywood piece
installed in the field. Tall oven cabinets:
standard

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:11.900
cutout. Standard cutout oven cabinets labeled O
for single cutouts and OM for oven microwave

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:17.400
combinations are available in both Shiloh and
Eclipse. In Eclipse, you can order them

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:23.000
with or without an overlay frame. With overlay
frames, the cutout must be at least 3 inches

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:28.300
narrower than the cabinet width to allow for the
frame stiles to each be at least 1.5

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:34.000
inches wide. For example, a 30-inch wide cabinet
would not be able to have a cutout larger

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:41.000
than 27 inches wide. However, if you are using a
cabinet without an overlay frame, the cabinet

00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:46.800
width can often match the appliance width
exactly. So, for example, a 30-inch wide cabinet

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:52.500
can house a 30-inch wide oven, overlay versus no
overlay examples. Here you can see the

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:58.500
difference. With an overlay panel, a 30-inch
wide oven is installed in a 33-inch wide oven

00:02:58.500 --> 00:03:03.200
cabinet. On the right, without an overlay panel,
the cabinet itself can be 30 inches

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:09.600
wide to match the appliance. Tall oven cabinets,
flush inset. Flush inset oven cabinets are

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:14.700
available in both Shiloh and Eclipse. In these
the outer frame surrounds the appliance, so

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:20.300
it sits flush with the cabinet face. Ordering
requires careful attention. You must specify

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:25.000
both the outer overlay frame and the inner
subframe dimensions on the flush inset cutout

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:30.900
sheet. Here we see two examples of flush inset
oven cabinets in framed and frameless cabinetry.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:35.800
The picture on the left shows a flush inset oven
microwave cabinet in Shiloh inset construction

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:40.900
cabinetry. The picture on the right shows a
flush inset oven cabinet in eclipse frameless

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:47.000
cabinetry. Wall Microwave Custom Cabinets. For
wall microwave custom cabinets, standard

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:54.200
depths are 18, 21, and 24 inches with an
additional 16-inch depth option in Eclipse. The
interior

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:59.100
is always unfinished and you must include the
exact cutout width and height on the cutout

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:05.100
sheet and include with your order. Base
Appliance Cabinets. Base oven cabinets and base
warming

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:09.800
drawer cabinets differ mainly in their lower
storage. Base oven cabinets typically have

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:15.200
one drawer or no drawers if using a taller
appliance. While warming drawer-based cabinets

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:20.600
will have two drawers. But the naming shouldn't
limit you. You can use any built-in appliance

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:25.800
in either style. As an example, the most common
appliance used on a base oven cabinet is a

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:31.400
drawer microwave. As with all appliance
cabinets, remember to include all cutout
dimensions

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:36.600
on your cutout sheet and include with your
order. Here are a few examples. A standard

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:41.800
base oven cutout in Shiloh inset cabinetry, a
standard tall oven microwave cabinet with

00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:47.000
no overlay in eclipse cabinetry, and a wall
microwave custom cabinet.

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.400
Order forms.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:52.500
Every appliance cutout order must include the
correct appliance cutout worksheet available

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:58.300
in the resources section of our dealer portal at
my.wwinc.com.

00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:02.900
This ensures accurate manufacturing and a
perfect fit for your appliances.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:06.800
By understanding these options and providing
complete, accurate information on your order

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:13.000
forms, you can confidently design appliance
cabinets that fit perfectly and look beautiful.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:16.700
Thank you for watching and happy designing with
WW wood products.
